"use client";
/**
 * Gestion Calendrier (source L25427–L26098, v65): domain model (time-zone maths in an explicit IANA zone, availability
 * engine, conflict detection, idempotent booking revalidated at commit, weekly recurrence with overrides, lifecycle with
 * an explicit transition table, integration events, notification outbox with simulated delivery, ICS import / export,
 * public booking links), synthetic seed, the application shell (HR & Payroll component classes), agenda (day / work week
 * / week / month / list; by time, practitioner or room), 9-step booking wizard, drawer, drag-and-drop rescheduling,
 * requests, planning, series, availability, resources, notifications, external calendars, online booking, settings,
 * audit, and the integrations with Patients (record cards and actions), Billing (appointments to bill) and Cabinet.
 *
 * Deliberate structure (ADR-04 exception, as for HR, Billing and Patients): typed imperative island filling the
 * `.hr.clapp` container. The code below is the source's own text with types added; the OS integration (L26082–L26097)
 * is replaced by src/apps/calendar/CalendarApp.tsx. Module-level integrations (Patients hooks, bus consumers) are
 * installed by clInstallIntegrations(), called only when the healthcare suite runs natively (see healthNative()).
 *
 * Simulated as in the source (S class): roles are a browser-side demo; every appointment is synthetic; message delivery
 * is simulated (no SMS / e-mail provider is connected); public booking pages are previewed inside the app.
 */
